---
// src/components/Sections/Home/WhatIsAMakerspace.astro — "What is a makerspace / hackerspace?".
// Copy carried over from the old brisbanemaker.space homepage.
import SectionHeading from "@components/Sections/Global/SectionHeading.astro";
import { PixelPanel } from "@components/ui/pixel-panel";
import { Reveal } from "@components/ui/reveal";

const link = "text-info hover:text-success underline transition-colors";
---

<Reveal as="section" aria-labelledby="makerspace-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-6">
  <SectionHeading id="makerspace-heading" title="What is a makerspace?" />
  <PixelPanel class="flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 md:p-8">
    <p class="text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed">
      A makerspace or hackerspace generally refer to the same thing. To quote <a
        href="https://hackerspaces.org"
        class={link}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">hackerspaces.org</a
      >, they are “community-operated physical places, where people share their interest in tinkering
      with technology, meet and work on their projects, and learn from each other.”
    </p>
    <p class="text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed">
      We think the phrase “makerspace” is more inclusive and friendly than “hackerspace” as the latter
      often has a negative connotation. There are several makerspaces or hackerspaces in Brisbane. We
      hope to differentiate ourselves by fostering a friendly and engaging community that is fun to be a
      part of.
    </p>
    <p class="text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed">
      Whether you want to call it a hackerspace or makerspace, we think everyone will have a great time
      and make new connections. We encourage you to come along to one of our social events or community
      open nights to learn more and see what all the fuss is about!
    </p>
  </PixelPanel>
</Reveal>
